@packages/lsp/_module.sigil from SigilLsp import { Markdown, consumer component, LanguageFeatures }
@integrations/editor/vscode/_module.sigil from SigilVsCodeExtension import { DocumentPreview }
component SigilVsCodeE2ETester {
  goal {
    Verify the VS Code integration through an *isolated extension host*.

    Exercise editor commands and observable compiler integration behavior at the VS
    Code API boundary without depending on a user's *global editor state*.
  }

  constraints {
    TestRunner {
      uses @vscode/test-electron to launch a separate *VS Code extension host*

      disables unrelated extensions and supplies a *temporary test workspace* or
      controlled fixture state

      uses current built language and *native compiler executables* for real design and alignment
      checks and diagnostic assertions; separate unit fixtures
      exercise all state/exit pairs without invoking a model

      does not mutate the repository's user workspace or depend on *global VS Code*
      settings
    }
  }

  cases {

    Navigate a real selected provider Tag, preserving consumer component hover
    context and owner definition.

    Exercise supplementary *Unicode positions* and CRLF in both LSP positions and
    native *byte-range diagnostics*, including related locations; stale
    source digest prevents location publication.

    Current native fixtures use design report 6 and alignment report 1 with *compatible stored readings*
    produced outside the editor command. The retained legacy skill fixture remains
    a separately selected 0.7 check.
    ExtensionHostLifecycle {
      the tester starts the extension host, discovers the Sigil extension, waits
      until hover and definition providers respond for the fixture, and exits with a
        passing result after all *test assertions*

      an extension activation, readiness, or *assertion* failure exits the test run
      with the failing assertion and captured host output
    }

    Opening a Sigil fixture uses LanguageFeatures through the VS Code command API
    for
    hover and definition.

    FileCompilationCommand {
      Compile File checks an *active physical Sigil* source in design focus, or
      checks the configured workspace selection in implementation focus and filters
      its code diagnostics to the active file. Native findings carry verified
      source ranges. Missing design or code readings keep the check Incomplete. The
      obsolete component alias is not registered.
    }

    ExternalCompilerFailure {
      a missing native executable returns no *successful report*, writes the failure
      to
      Sigil output, clears previous findings and shows actionable error text
    }

    DirtyDocument {
      invoking Compile File for an unsaved Sigil document does not start the external
      compiler and shows a *warning* asking the user to save the document
    }

    invoking Open Preview through the command API exercises DocumentPreview and
    opens a Markdown preview for the whole active Sigil document

    TestIsolation {
      unrelated installed extensions and the user's *global compiler executable* do
      not
      determine the command-contract assertions
    }
  }

  interface {
    ExtensionHostTest {
      launches the *extension development host* with the Sigil integration and a
      controlled file-backed workspace

      invokes contributed language, preview, and *compilation* commands through the
      VS
      Code command API

      inspects native selection, *named states*, structured output and ranged diagnostics
    }
  }
}
